    },
    {
      "Kind": "text",
      "Section": "Why Use Organization Authorizations?",
      "Anchor": "why-use-organization-authorizations",
      "SectionPath": [
        "Role Checking Types",
        "Why Use Organization Authorizations?"
      ],
      "Text": "The /organizationAuthorizations endpoint provides a way to determine if a user has access to a particular feature without needing to know which roles the user has.",
      "Headers": [],
      "Rows": []
    },
    {
      "Kind": "text",
      "Section": "Why Use Organization Authorizations?",
      "Anchor": "why-use-organization-authorizations",
      "SectionPath": [
        "Role Checking Types",
        "Why Use Organization Authorizations?"
      ],
      "Text": "When using /organizationAcls, every new Role introduced by LinkedIn will require additional checks for each of your user\u0027s permissions. For example, if you\u0027re checking /organizationAcls \u0022isAdmin\u0022 to determine whether or not they can post as the company, you\u0027ll need to also check is admin || content admin || each time a new role is released.",
      "Headers": [],
      "Rows": []
    },
    {
      "Kind": "text",
      "Section": "Role to Permission Mapping",
      "Anchor": "role-to-permission-mapping",
      "SectionPath": [
        "Role to Permission Mapping"
      ],
      "Text": "Each Role is authorized to perform a certain behavior which is mapped to a list of permissions with same OrganizationAuthorizationAction, or permission type.",
      "Headers": [],
      "Rows": []
    },
